# Force LF line endings in the working tree on every platform.
#
# GitHub-hosted windows-latest runners check out with core.autocrlf=true (CRLF).
# scripts/node-text-linter.mjs begins with a `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang, and a
# shebang line + CRLF makes that .mjs fail to PARSE under vitest on Windows with
# "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" — the whole file collects zero tests.
# Reproduced deterministically: CRLF + shebang fails; CRLF without the shebang parses;
# LF (either way) parses. The shebang is load-bearing (the file is a runnable CLI),
# so the fix is to guarantee LF at checkout everywhere rather than drop the shebang.
#
# As a bonus this makes checkout bytes == committed bytes on every OS, so any future
# line-ending-sensitive step (e.g. a `git diff --exit-code` codegen gate) stays honest.
* text=auto eol=lf
